   "text": {
    "L1": "In Paper Boats, a child floats a paper boat each day.",
    "L2": "He writes his name and village on it, so someone far away may know him.",
    "L3": "The boat carries his hope of finding a friend and connecting with others.",
    "L4": "At night, the stars steer his boats in the poem. This personification creates an image of hope and imagination.",
    "L5": "MYTH: The stars really steer boats. NOT TRUE—the poet gives stars a human action to show the child's imagination.",
    "L6": "Now notice the grammar: the boy floats his boats, but his friends watch them.",
    "L7": "For one person, the verb takes -s. With a plural subject, the verb does not take -s.",
    "L8": "Choose the verb that completes the sentence about the boy."
   },
